Metrics List:
- {"name": "container_memory_usage_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Current memory usage in bytes, including all memory regardless of when it was accessed"}
- {"name": "container_memory_max_usage_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Maximum memory usage recorded in bytes"}
- {"name": "container_memory_failcnt", "type": "counter", "description": "Number of memory usage hits limits"}
- {"name": "kube_statefulset_status_replicas_current", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] The number of current replicas per StatefulSet."}
- {"name": "container_cpu_usage_seconds_total", "type": "counter", "description": "Cumulative cpu time consumed in seconds."}
- {"name": "container_blkio_device_usage_total", "type": "counter", "description": "Blkio Device bytes usage"}
- {"name": "container_fs_usage_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of bytes that are consumed by the container on this filesystem."}
- {"name": "container_memory_working_set_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Current working set in bytes."}
- {"name": "node_disk_io_now", "type": "gauge", "description": "The number of I/Os currently in progress."}
- {"name": "kube_pod_container_status_running", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] Describes whether the container is currently in running state."}
- {"name": "node_forks_total", "type": "counter", "description": "Total number of forks."}
- {"name": "node_memory_HugePages_Total", "type": "gauge", "description": "Memory information field HugePages_Total."}
- {"name": "container_memory_failures_total", "type": "counter", "description": "Cumulative count of memory allocation failures."}
- {"name": "node_context_switches_total", "type": "counter", "description": "Total number of context switches."}
Question: Among all pods of the admin route service, which one has the highest total memory usage summed across all its containers? Show its current total memory usage.
